\f1\fs22 While Chanta thought the Jones clones were developing hobbies, they were, in fact, developing a Grand Unified Conspiracy Theory. He might have wised up if he\'92d noticed their propensity to find exotic patterns in everything, and even more exotic theories for the causes of those patterns. If knew what the word \'91\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
apophenia\'92 meant, or the curiosity to look it up in a dictionary or more gumption to find one than merely ask the Elvisettes in anyone had one in their handbag or toiletry kits\'97which face, he never got even that far anyway\'97he might have twigged to the behaviour.\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\fs24 \cf2 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
<!$Scr_Ps::0><$Scr_Ps::1>
\f1\fs22 Chanta didn\'92t notice when a Jones clone discovered the box of corn flakes was sitting at a \'93suspicious angle\'94 in the pantry one morning, which launched a whole investigation, complete with setting evidence numbers alongside staple pantry items like a jar of peanut butter, five Tim Tams, and a packet of forty-eight-year-old crumpets. He didn\'92t ask why they were dusting the pantry for prints, or why they were fastidiously measuring the angles between breakfast cereal boxes looking for hidden pentagrams. He didn\'92t wonder about conversations between them that involved phrases like, \'93You will count the cornflakes\'94, or the conspiratorial arrangement of the spice rack, or the presence of a broken ring-pull on a tomato tin and its implications for national security.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0
\cf2 Perhaps worst of all, Chanta never realised they had started gathering around a TV in a library on the western side of the penthouse, where they stood passively yet alert, with backs against walls and hands clasped in front, and reverently watched old episodes of 
\f2\i The Moe Bogan Experience
\f1\i0  on Boo Choob.\
That stuff was catnip for their paranoia.\
It started because a Jones clone had noticed that the streaming service was already operating on the TV with an account named 
\f2\i BigKnackers66
\f1\i0 . 
\f2\i  
\f1\i0 The account history revealed an almost exclusive adherence to 
\f2\i The Experience
\f1\i0 . The Jones clone immediately called for back up.\
Watching the 
\f2\i Moe Bogan Experience 
\f1\i0 quickly became religious.\
Late one evening, after all the staff were present and accounted for in their quarters, a full congregation of the Jones clones attended the library and surveilled the TV from their vantage points against the walls. They watched the eponymous Bogan chat to a fungal ecologist who had renounced ecology some years earlier as a money-laundering scam, and narrowed his study to mushrooms. The apostate anti-ecologist, who claimed to be at one with the mushroom, was explaining why mushrooms knew things.\
\'93See, that\'92s what people don\'92t get,\'94 Bogan inserted at one point, when his guest finally stopped for a breath. \'93They think intelligence has to be in a head.\'94\
\'93Exactly.\'94\
\'93But mycelium doesn\'92t have a head.\'94\
\'93Exactly.\'94\
\'93So who\'92s thinking?\'94\
The guest went on to say that fungal networks could propagate information without any individual part understanding the whole.\
\'93If you put ten thousand genomically identical brains together,\'94 he said, \'93everybody calls it a crowd. I\'92d rather think  it\'92s one brain with ten thousand heads.\'94\
By the following afternoon, folding tables appeared in a penthouse-sized sauna. The Jones clones liked the acoustics and had assessed the walls to be mostly ballistically repellant. The tables grew laptops and monitors.The sauna became a command centre.\
They fed an under weight artificial mediocrity model with the transcripts of every episode of 
\f2\i The Moe Bogan Experience
\f1\i0 . Then they read it the  transcripts in case vocal emphasis might clarify  interpretation. They checked the qualifications of the guests, and who had issued those qualifications. They searched for deleted episodes and ran thorough investigations when they found one.\
And they kept gathering in the library to watch episodes. It was spiritual, until one of the clones argued they shouldn\'92t skip advertisements.\
They started to have conversations that included observations like, \'93If a Jones network exists, agreement between Joneses cannot be used as evidence for a Jones network.\'94\
They ordered more computers.\
Fisher discovered the operation when an accounts clerk asked if he should create a new cost centre for \'93Jones Investigations\'94. He quickly found the library in which they congregated, though it took him slightly longer to find them in the sauna. He stole into their quarters in the middle of the day and found reports hidden in pillow cases with titles like 
\fs20 \'93
\f3\b GRAYLING PRODUCT VARIATION \'97 POSSIBLE SIGNIFICANCE OF TIE COLOUR\'94
\f1\b0\fs22 \
The Jones clones continued to watch eps of 
\f2\i The Experience
\f1\i0 . Some of them they watched twice.\
A former government analyst appeared on the program and explained that people misunderstood the Deep State.\
\'93It isn\'92t deep,\'94 he said. \'93It\'92s mycelial.\'94\
A Jones clone drew a doubled-headed arrow on a chart connecting the words DEEP STATE and MUSHROOMS. They drew more lines on more charts. GRAYLING connected to PAPER connected to Government.\
And HIBReLabs, Shakti, Fridge Force.\
By the middle of the following week, cables snaked into the sauna and crossed the floor under rubber mats. Headphones hung from chairs. Transcripts accumulated in boxes. Competing diagrams overlapped on the walls.\
One whiteboard carried two headings.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f3\b \cf2 BIOLOGICAL NETWORK
\f1\b0 \

\f3\b INSTITUTIONAL NETWORK
\f1\b0 \
Arrows connected both headings to the hastily ringed word, MYCELIAL.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sl220\sb220\qj\partightenfactor0

